{"availability":"available","full":"Cartograf666/concert-for-travelers-api","name":"concert-for-travelers-api","description":"Fully autonomous, self-healing concert-scraping network (90+ venues + Ticketmaster + Bandsintown) publishing a free static JSON API. Zero servers, zero manual ops.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-06T21:19:28Z","updated":"2026-10-08T12:38:17Z","license":"ISC","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cartograf666.github.io/concert-for-travelers-api/","topics":["concerts","gemini-api","github-actions","github-pages","json-api","nodejs","self-healing","static-site","typescript","web-scraping"],"demo":"https://cartograf666.github.io/concert-for-travelers-api/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.758Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.758Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.758Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.758Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fully autonomous, self-healing pipeline that scrapes concerts from 90+ venues, Ticketmaster, Bandsintown, and Eventbrite; matches them against a 63,000+ artist whitelist; enriches artist metadata via free structured sources and Gemini; and publishes it all as a free static JSON API. Zero servers, zero manual intervention in the normal case.","This repo is backend/data-only — no frontend. A separate app, concerts-for-travelers, consumes the JSON published here to answer one question: \"Which of the artists I love are playing where I'll be, and when?\""],"features":["Zero-Ops, Fully Autonomous Architecture — runs entirely inside GitHub Actions and deploys statically to GitHub Pages. No database, no server, no manual intervention in the normal case: scrape, discover, enrich, heal,…","Layered, Free-First Artist Enrichment Cascade — website + socials (Spotify/Instagram/Facebook/YouTube/Telegram/VK) are filled in via, in order of cost: a bulk Wikidata SPARQL sweep (80 names/query), a per-artist…","Multi-Key Gemini Failover — both enrichment and self-healing rotate through every configured key (GEMINIAPIKEY, 2..10, RESERV1..10, or a bulk GEMINIAPIKEYS list) and a model cascade (Gemma → Gemini Flash tiers), moving…","Tiered Artist Whitelist Matching — exact match → whole-word cover/tribute-band filter → coverage-guarded substring match (with an attached-capitalized-neighbor guard so a short entry can't absorb a fragment of a longer,…","Self-Healing CSS Selectors, Auto-Merged — when a scraper stops returning concerts, an automated flow asks Gemini (structured output, restricted to selector fields — never the venue/city/country fallbacks) to repair it,…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Cartograf666/concert-for-travelers-api/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"21b0cdc3bb852df0e8f5359eaf93f1c940bcea5525b407f5ca8e3c46797bffd5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.913Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.913Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A fully autonomous, self-healing pipeline that scrapes concerts from 90+ venues, Ticketmaster, Bandsintown, and Eventbrite; matches them against a 63,000+ artist whitelist; enriches artist metadata via free structured sources and Gemini; and publishes it all as a free static JSON API. Zero servers, zero manual intervention in the normal case.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Cartograf666/concert-for-travelers-api/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"A Gemini API Key (optional, needed for JIT enrichment & self-healing)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Cartograf666/concert-for-travelers-api/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"21b0cdc3bb852df0e8f5359eaf93f1c940bcea5525b407f5ca8e3c46797bffd5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Cartograf666/concert-for-travelers-api/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:58.913Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T12:38:17Z","readmeSnapsho